
# URSOY raw source data (~10 GB, fetched by tools/island_fetch.js)
assets/island/raw/

# Terrain bench scratch bakes (tools/terrain_bake.js --out) and the island
# preps (tools/island_prep.py): a developer artefact, reproducible from the raw
# set — see tools/_terrain.html, tools/_island.html.
#
# READ THIS BEFORE PUTTING ANYTHING THE GAME LOADS HERE (2026-09-23). This rule
# was written on 2026-09-04 for scratch, ten days before the island existed.
# Jolene's bake was then written into bench/jolene and bench/terrain and
# inherited it — so the DEFAULT MAP was in no clone, no worktree and no cloud
# session for nine days, GATE WORLD skipped its eight island checks in silence,
# and two junction workarounds emptied bench/ outright. The world ships now, as
# it was always meant to (ISLAND-PREPACK §5b): tools/world_prep.js gzips the
# seventeen layers the game reads into media/world/<id> under content-hashed
# names and lists them in src/core/world_packs.json.
#
# So: bench/ is the BAKE'S INPUT and nothing else. If the game fetches it, it
# belongs in media/ through a manifest bake, not here.
bench/

# Screenshots (2026-09-14, user ruling): bench and game captures are
# developer evidence, reproducible from the rigs that took them, not a
# shipped asset. The ones already committed stay in history; new captures
# are not picked up.
screenshots/
# the pilot matrix's run files (tools/pilot_matrix.js --out): measurements, not sources
pilot_runs/
